From 269e919bb5e6d1e870ff0653c753e087077d79e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Samuel Price <thesamprice@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:10:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] bsps/microblaze: Link with --no-relax

GCC passes -relax to the linker for microblaze*-*-rtems*.  With
relaxation, ld deletes the IMM prefix of instructions whose operand fits
in 16 bits and shifts the following code.  Several things that encode
code offsets as assembly-time constants are not adjusted for this.  The
one that breaks applications is the C++ exception call-site table in
.gcc_except_table: GCC writes the call-site start, length and landing
pad offsets as .uleb128 differences of code labels, which the assembler
resolves without a relocation.  When relaxation shrinks a function, the
unwinder uses the old offsets, lands in the wrong place and hangs or
calls std::terminate().  With GCC 15.2 and binutils 2.47,
samples/cdtest hangs after its first caught exception.  The bug is
older than binutils 2.47: with the binutils 2.36 the RTEMS 7 tools
still use, it shows up whenever an IMM inside a function with a
try/catch is deleted.

Pass --no-relax in the ABI flags of the microblaze_fpga family, after
the -relax from GCC, so that the linker does not relax.  The ABI flags
are also in the BSP's pkg-config file, so applications get them too.
This costs about 3.5% of code size (the text of the sptests and samples
grows by 3.5% in total, samples/hello from 250008 to 258780 bytes).

A fix for binutils is in preparation:

https://github.com/thesamprice/microblaze-testsuite/tree/main/patches/series/binutils-microblaze-eh-relax

Revert this once the RTEMS tools use a binutils with the fix.

Assisted-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml b/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml
index 7d78c9842d..eb842ecd14 100644
--- a/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml
+++ b/spec/build/bsps/microblaze/microblaze_fpga/abi.yml
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ default:
   - -mno-xl-soft-div
   - -mno-xl-soft-mul
   - -Wl,-EL
+  - -Wl,--no-relax
 description: |
   ABI flags
 enabled-by: true
-- 
2.39.5 (Apple Git-154)

